**Score Bands**

| **Score** | **Level** | **What It Means** |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **10 – 20** | **Starter** | Using AI occasionally in default mode. Most value still locked. |
| **21 – 30** | **User** | Getting real value but leaving most on the table. A few fixes will change this fast. |
| **31 – 40** | **Builder** | Solid setup with clear intent. A few gaps worth closing. |
| **41 – 50** | **Operator** | AI is a genuine multiplier. Built deliberately and it shows. |

**What each dimension gap means for you**

Any dimension scoring 4 or below: treat as HIGH priority. Fixing a low-scoring dimension is typically worth more than marginal improvements to a high one.

**01  Profile (score 1–4)**

You're starting every conversation cold. AI has no idea who you are, what your role needs, or how you communicate best. Fix: spend 30 minutes writing a role profile for each major tool you use — role, context, communication style, goals, what not to do.

**02  Tools (score 1–4)**

You're using a general-purpose hammer for every task. Different tools are built for different jobs. Fix: audit what you actually do in a week, then map each job to the right tool. Stop using ChatGPT for everything.

**03  Workflow (score 1–4)**

AI is an occasional add-on, not part of how you work. Fix: identify your top 3 most repetitive tasks this week. Build a prompt + workflow for each one. Use them for 5 days. That's the install.

**04  Prompting (score 1–4)**

You're getting generic outputs because you're giving generic inputs. Fix: learn one framework (role + context + task + format + constraints) and apply it to every single request for one week. The quality jump will be immediate.

**05  Integrations (score 1–4)**

AI is a standalone tab you open and close. Fix: install 2–3 plugins that connect AI to where you actually work — your email, your calendar, your docs. Start with the app you open most.

